{"clock":1,"nonce":"cc475324381a2ba0aab28368e82465e4","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793223589,"data":{"body":"One verb per side and starting over landed with #66 (c51b7f5, 2026-10-28; PRD `docs/prd/sync-sides.md`). This issue collects what's left: two follow-ups that each need their own design, the minor findings #66's review deferred, and two bits of housekeeping.\n\n## Two follow-ups, each with its own design\n\n- **A forge pull that adopts git-board's markers.** `byMarker` (`core/syncer/sync.go`) skips a forge issue whose git-board marker names an id the board doesn't have, and comments go the same way (`core/syncer/plan.go`). So after a start-over, what git-board itself posted to a forge doesn't come back. On a repository with two forges, such as the wiki, the copies on the second forge don't join their issue again either. Until then, starting over is safe only where git-board never posted to a forge: not the wiki, git-board-test or co2-calculator.\n- **Release records from GitHub releases.** A reset loses the release records (`refs/board/release`), and GitHub keeps a release for 10 of this repository's 17. Import them, and decide whether the records and GitHub's releases stay in step afterwards.\n\n## Deferred from #66's review\n\n- [ ] `NumberIssues` pushes `refs/board/seq` without the reset mark's guard (`internal/store/numbers.go`).\n- [ ] Settings › Sync's Fetch shows the counts without the guard's warning (`internal/server/remotes.go`). Its Pull does refuse, with the message.\n- [ ] With no git remote at all, Start over's reset card can't be confirmed: the name to type is origin's (`web/src/remotes.ts`).\n- [ ] The server holds `forgeMu` across a network `push --prune` or take, so the status polls wait meanwhile (`internal/server/startover.go`).\n- [ ] An error after the backup bundle is written drops the bundle's path from the output (`cmd/git-board/reset.go`, `internal/server/startover.go`).\n- [ ] Settings › Sync's Project Push is enabled on a read-only Project, and silently skips every edit.\n\n## Housekeeping\n\n- [ ] `TestInputsAreChecked` (`internal/store/store_test.go:204`) fails about 2% of runs: when a random id's first 8 hex digits are all digits, `strings.ToUpper` changes nothing, and the prefix resolves.\n- [ ] `CLAUDE.md` says `refs/bugs` holds this repository's issues, which is stale since the switch.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The two follow-ups each have their own issue.\n- [ ] Each deferred finding is fixed, or closed with a reason.\n- [ ] The flaky test passes every time, and `CLAUDE.md` no longer names `refs/bugs`.\n","title":"sync: follow-ups after one verb per side (#66)"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793223589,"data":{"add":["assignee:guilbep","kind:feat","prio:p2","status:backlog"],"remove":null}}]}